tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:1:20:error:CleanProse.NoForceWords:§2: 'try to' states no force. If the force is conditional, write a Conditional sentence. Otherwise, write a force word.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:4:1:error:CleanProse.NoForceWords:§2: 'It is a good idea to' states no force. If the force is conditional, write a Conditional sentence. Otherwise, write a force word.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:4:1:suggestion:CleanProse.VagueAntecedent:§1: 'It is' opens on a bare pronoun. If the pronoun's referent is not the previous sentence's subject, name the noun. If the sentence only justifies the one before it and §8 does not keep the reason, cut the sentence per §7.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:7:1:warning:CleanProse.ThroatClearing:§7: 'This section explains' announces text instead of stating a rule. Cut it.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:10:5:suggestion:CleanProse.LowercaseForce:§2: 'need to' is outside the force vocabulary. If it states obligation, permission, or preference, write the force word (MUST, NEVER, SHOULD, MAY, PREFER X OVER Y). If it does not, leave it.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:13:27:suggestion:CleanProse.VagueAntecedent:§1: 'This keeps' opens on a bare pronoun. If the pronoun's referent is not the previous sentence's subject, name the noun. If the sentence only justifies the one before it and §8 does not keep the reason, cut the sentence per §7.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:16:19:suggestion:CleanProse.ConditionLast:§1: the condition follows the action. Write 'If C, do X', not 'Do X if C'.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:28:14:suggestion:CleanProse.ConditionLast:§1: the condition follows the action. Write 'If C, do X', not 'Do X if C'.
